<table>
<tr><th>Part</th><th>Meaning</th></tr>
<tr><td>protected</td><td>Callable from subclass / same package (child can invoke on parent’s clone)</td></tr>
<tr><td>native</td><td>Not implemented in Java — JVM/platform native code</td></tr>
<tr><td>Return type Object</td><td>Returns duplicate as Object reference</td></tr>
<tr><td>throws CloneNotSupportedException</td><td>Checked exception — must catch or declare</td></tr>
</table>
<table>
<tr><th>Type</th><th>Who implements</th></tr>
<tr><td>Shallow</td><td>`Object.clone()` (via super.clone())</td></tr>
<tr><td>Deep</td><td>Programmer — override clone(), create nested copies manually</td></tr>
</table>
<table>
<tr><th>Object shape</th><th>Best choice</th></tr>
<tr><td>Only primitive instance fields</td><td>Shallow cloning sufficient (Object.clone())</td></tr>
<tr><td>Contains reference fields (contained objects)</td><td>Deep cloning recommended (custom clone())</td></tr>
</table>
